# Character reference photos

## Location
- Canonical folder: `lessons/assets/refs/george/`
- Full tag index: `lessons/assets/refs/george/CATALOG.md`
- Photos in this folder are **tracked in git** (for shared agent / illustrator access)
- Put new photos **directly** into `lessons/assets/refs/george/` and update `CATALOG.md` (do not use `ref/`)

## Cast ids (use these names in filenames and story art)
- `george` — boy ~5, lesson hero (short black hair with bangs, round face)
- `daddy` — father (short dark hair, usually thin glasses)
- `mummy` — mother
- `sylvia` — older sister (often cap / ponytail)

## Filename pattern
`{subjects}-{setting}-{pose-or-mood}[-variant].jpg`  
Example: `george-daddy-outdoors-lifevest-smile.jpg` (George listed first)

## When generating lesson illustrations
1. Open `CATALOG.md`, then **Read** the chosen photo(s) before drawing
2. Default George likeness: `george-solo-bed-smile.jpg` (`priority: primary`); strong face/cover ref: `george-solo-sofa-alphabet-smile.jpg`
3. Daddy face: `george-daddy-outdoors-pavilion-neutral.jpg`
4. Match cast + mood tags from the catalog to the story beat
5. Keep George consistent across the whole lesson; do not invent a different child face
6. Never embed these private photos in published HTML; only AI/drawn picture-book art goes under `lessons/assets/lesson-XX/`

## AI voice (paired with likeness)
- Fixed voice per cast id: see `scripts/voices.json` and `docs/character-voices.md`
- George → `george`, Daddy → `daddy`; dragons Pip / Ember → `pip` / `ember`
